- Writing append-only JSONL records (manifest/audit/event streams)  
- Loading a worklist (IDs) from a manifest JSONL file  
- Choosing an active manifest (baseline vs retry) based on retry file presence  
  
Inputs  
------  
- manifest_path: Path to a JSONL file where each line is a JSON object  
- manifest_key_field: field name that contains the work item ID (e.g., "key_ID")  
- baseline_manifest: baseline manifest path (e.g., data/manifest.jsonl)  
- retry_manifest: retry manifest path (e.g., data/manifest_retry.jsonl)  
- audit_log_path: JSONL audit log path  
- record: dict payloads for append/write_audit  
  
Outputs  
-------  
- Appends JSONL lines to provided paths  
- Returns list[str] of IDs when loading from a manifest  
- Returns Path of the chosen active manifest  
  
When to use  
-----------  
- You already have a manifest JSONL (or will produce one elsewhere) and need:  
  - consistent JSONL append semantics  
  - robust ID loading  
  - retry-manifest selection for resumable runs  
  
When NOT to use  
---------------  
- You need a database-backed queue, concurrency control, or transactional updates.  
- You want to build manifests from Excel/CSV/API sources (belongs to INPUT milestone).  
  
Headless notes  
--------------  
- Headless-agnostic; no browser interaction.  
  
Dependencies  
------------  
- Standard library only: json, datetime, pathlib, typing, logging  
  
Common failure modes + mitigations  
----------------------------------  
- Missing manifest file -> FileNotFoundError (caller should create or guard).  
- Corrupt JSONL lines -> json.JSONDecodeError (validate upstream writers).  
- Audit write failures -> optionally swallowed to avoid failing the run.  
  
